{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/89488-questions-about-the-shadow-angst-and-npcs","id":89488,"title":"Questions about the Shadow, Angst, and NPCs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-12T08:06:59-07:00","id":89488,"title":"Questions about the Shadow, Angst, and NPCs","content":"Okay so its insanely easy to build up Angst in the game, and much of the Governments of all the Dark Kingdoms are sinister as Hell. So how does for instance a Judge of the Dead in the Dark Kingdom of Jade maintain the fight with their P'o when they regularly deal out merciless sentences? Like Li Gao one of the 4 Magistrates retains his position by being merciless.<br /> <br /> This leads me to question if why can't you have individuals who are in harmony with their shadow? Why can't you have someone who trusts their shadow more then anyone, while at the same time the Shadow returns the trust. This is particularly something I would expect out of certain enlightened individuals, though I guess they are more likely to transcend.<br /> <br /> This is also why I wish it wasn't so Black and white with the Wraiths vs Specters/Shadow. Many of the NPCs honestly feel like they should be Specters that still work with society. For instance as mentioned with the Dark Kingdom of Jade, if you are a high ranking official you can't get away with going crazy every now and then due to your P'o gaining control, you would likely need to make a deal, particularly if you both want to avoid being turned into building material for failing a high pressure job. How do the Deathlords survive? Pretty much anyone in high positions of control or even fame regularly would accumulate Angst as a matter of daily routine.<br /> <br /> I think I would like it better if it was say like in Exalted where you didn't have the Wraith/Specter divide as a crunch thing, instead you get some wraiths are pleasant and some are utter douchers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T08:42:00-07:00","id":89507,"title":"","content":"Castigate and Way of the Soul (for Jade Kingdom), I have always attributed long running NPC and PC survival as being based on regular doses of one of these Arcanoi. Way of the Soul obviously being better at it the Castigate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T21:51:51-07:00","id":95402,"title":"","content":"Also, I believe it's possible to be just a complete asshole and not build up Angst. So for instance if your Passions are Punish the Wicked (Justice 5) and your corresponding Dark Passion is Turn a Blind Eye (Cowardice 3), NOT dealing severe punishments would get your Angst to ratchet up faster. Note Passions are not necessarily &quot;good&quot; and Dark Passions are not necessarily &quot;bad&quot;. Passions are simply those emotions and drives that the character openly accepts about themself, while Dark Passions are the drives they try to deny exist. The ghosts of a white civil rights reformer and a early 20th century Southern sheriff might have the same Passions and Dark Passions, only flipped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T22:53:40-07:00","id":95422,"title":"","content":"Exactly. The Shadow Player's Guide talks about it as less &quot;the Shadow is evil&quot; and more &quot;the Shadow is subversive and acts on the desires the wraith doesn't like having.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T06:34:24-07:00","id":96314,"title":"","content":"Wolfgar and atamajakki said it. I just thought id chime in...<br /> <br /> You have to be creative with your passions/dark passions to make things interesting, Not all wraiths are goody goodies, everything is in degrees. In my opinion, playing a good shadow is incredibly difficult (probably the most difficult in the CWoD universe) and in my troupe, im actually the only one allowed to play one (which kinda sucks because i like being a wraith too XD). Taking a good long time with passions is the key to a wraith/shadow. They are afterall the main reason they are still sticking around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2467-iris","name":"Iris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T23:39:44-07:00","id":96754,"title":"","content":"Almost no Wraith is a goody-goody. Wraiths are mostly drawn from the bulk of the World of Darkness general populace, and in such a crapsack world relatively few of them are an active force for good. Very few are diabolically evil either, but there will be a large number have an aberrant morality or are simply assholes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T13:00:32-07:00","id":97006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/89488-questions-about-the-shadow-angst-and-npcs?p=95402#post95402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I believe it's possible to be just a complete asshole and not build up Angst. So for instance if your Passions are Punish the Wicked (Justice 5) and your corresponding Dark Passion is Turn a Blind Eye (Cowardice 3), NOT dealing severe punishments would get your Angst to ratchet up faster. Note Passions are not necessarily &quot;good&quot; and Dark Passions are not necessarily &quot;bad&quot;. Passions are simply those emotions and drives that the character openly accepts about themself, while Dark Passions are the drives they try to deny exist. The ghosts of a white civil rights reformer and a early 20th century Southern sheriff might have the same Passions and Dark Passions, only flipped.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just had to quote this for its utter correctness. I have spent the past two decades trying to explain this to some people/players who just didn't &quot;get&quot; that a wraith's Passions (and other qualities) aren't necessarily positive (and often aren't), while the shadow's Dark Passions aren't always negative (that is, inherently &quot;eeeeeevvviillll&quot;, on the face of it -- they can be much more subtle and slyly corruptive, as opposed to more blatantly &quot;mwahaha&quot;...). A Wraith can be rather a dick, and have several rather harsh passions, while the shadow has more *seemingly* benign drives... but those drives gradually erode the strength/coherency of the wraith in question, and *that's* the &quot;negative&quot; involved in that spiritual equation. (Of course, more often than not, the wraith's drives *will be* more &quot;positive&quot; -- or at least relatively neutral -- as opposed to the shadow's more generally dark and corruptive ones, but it doesn't *always* have to be that way, and it is often quite more involved/complex a situation than meets the eye...).<br /> <br /> Good post, Wolfgar...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T02:38:00-07:00","id":97405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/89488-questions-about-the-shadow-angst-and-npcs?p=95402#post95402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I believe it's possible to be just a complete asshole and not build up Angst. So for instance if your Passions are Punish the Wicked (Justice 5) and your corresponding Dark Passion is Turn a Blind Eye (Cowardice 3), NOT dealing severe punishments would get your Angst to ratchet up faster. Note Passions are not necessarily &quot;good&quot; and Dark Passions are not necessarily &quot;bad&quot;. Passions are simply those emotions and drives that the character openly accepts about themself, while Dark Passions are the drives they try to deny exist. The ghosts of a white civil rights reformer and a early 20th century Southern sheriff might have the same Passions and Dark Passions, only flipped.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Exactly this.<br /> <br /> I had to run a vampire in a LARP I run dying and managing to successfully become a wraith (we have a system to see if it happens which is really hard, but possible). This vampire was on Path of Power and the Inner Voice and was, quite frankly, a violent psychotic bitch tyrant. So when I was talking with her to work out what her shadow would be like, her shadow ended up being a complete martyr trying to subvert her base nature through a desire to sacrifice herself for the good of others around her. It worked out beautifully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}